================================================================================
Protocol provenance and clean-room statement
================================================================================

Panelith talks to USB display panels from several vendors. None of these
vendors publish a protocol specification for the panels in question, with the
exception of BeadaPanel, which publishes an SDK.

The device protocol implementations in `src/Panelith.Devices` were written
from protocol *descriptions* -- byte layouts, command opcodes, handshake
sequences and pixel encodings -- that have been published by the hardware
reverse-engineering community. No source code was copied from any of the
projects listed below, several of which are GPL-licensed and therefore
incompatible with this project's Apache-2.0 license. Protocol facts (which byte
means what) are not themselves copyrightable; the expression of those facts in
this repository is original.

Projects whose published protocol documentation informed this implementation,
with thanks:

  * thermalright-lcd-control (Apache-2.0)
    https://github.com/rejeb/thermalright-lcd-control
    Documented the Thermalright/TRCC wire families: `ly` bulk, raw `bulk`,
    HID type 2 and type 3, SCSI/BOT, and the PM/SUB/FBL screen-identification
    tables used by the TRCC firmware.

  * turing-smart-screen-python (GPL-3.0)
    https://github.com/mathoudebine/turing-smart-screen-python
    Documented the Turing Smart Screen revision A/B/C/D serial command sets,
    the XuanFang variants, and the newer Turing USB bulk protocol.

  * InfoPanel (GPL-3.0)
    https://github.com/habibrehmansg/infopanel
    Documented panel behaviour, performance characteristics and the practical
    failure modes of these devices (see its PANELS.md).

  * liquidctl (GPL-3.0)
    https://github.com/liquidctl/liquidctl
    Documented all-in-one cooler LCD protocols.

Panelith is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Thermalright,
Turing, BeadaPanel, XuanFang, Kipye, WeAct Studio, or any other hardware
vendor. All trademarks are the property of their respective owners. Vendor and
model names appear in this project solely to identify hardware compatibility.

